BEGIN_HYPERDESC
<h1>Boosters into the sea at time acceleration</h1>
The two spent Space Shuttle boosters 3 km above the Atlantic, falling at
140 m/s, as saved from an ascent (the autopilot's) 40 s after separation;
the damage model on. They come down at 10x time acceleration (as a player
waiting for them would): each breaks up on the water, and what is left of
them must float, not spin up without bound. (A player's session ended in
a segmentation fault here: a booster's remains, with a twentieth of its
moment of inertia about its length, spun up until its state went
non-finite, and the swell's grid was indexed with it.)
END_HYPERDESC

